<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATCC4PFT/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATCC4PFT/>;
    dc:modified '2018-03-13T13:56:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'crops_of_c4_plant_functional_types'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The definition of "crops" is model dependent, for example, some models may include fruit trees as crops. A "c4 plant" is one that utilizes the C4 carbon fixation pathway in which the CO2 is first bound to a compound containing four carbon atoms before photosynthesis reactions take place. All trees are C3 type. Grasses and crops can be C3 or C4.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P29::ATCC4PFT'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATPC3PFT/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATPC3PFT/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATPC3PFT/>;
    dc:modified '2018-03-13T13:56:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'pastures_of_c3_plant_functional_types'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Pastures are assumed to be anthropogenic in origin. They include anthropogenically managed pastureland and rangeland. A "c3 plant" is one that utilizes the C3 carbon fixation pathway as the sole mechanism to bind CO2 before photosynthesis reactions take place. All trees are C3 type. Grasses and crops can be C3 or C4.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P29::ATPC3PFT'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATPC4PFT/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATPC4PFT/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATPC4PFT/>;
    dc:modified '2018-03-13T13:56:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'pastures_of_c4_plant_functional_types'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Pastures are assumed to be anthropogenic in origin. They include anthropogenically managed pastureland and rangeland. A "c4 plant" is one that utilizes the C4 carbon fixation pathway in which the CO2 is first bound to a compound containing four carbon atoms before photosynthesis reactions take place. All trees are C3 type. Grasses and crops can be C3 or C4.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P29::ATPC4PFT'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATSIRIDG/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATSIRIDG/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATSIRIDG/>;
    dc:modified '2018-03-13T13:56:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_ridges'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sea ice "ridging" occurs in rough sea conditions. The motion of the sea surface can cause areas of sea ice to deform and fold resulting in ridged upper and lower surfaces. The ridges can be as much as twenty metres thick if thick ice is deformed.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P29::ATSIRIDG'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATWETLND/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATWETLND/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATWETLND/>;
    dc:modified '2018-03-13T13:56:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'wetland'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Wetlands are areas where water covers the soil, or is present either at or near the surface of the soil all year or for varying periods of time during the year, including during the growing season.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P29::ATWETLND'^^xsd:string .
